Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer
3. Project Design Phase
3.1 System Architecture
The proposed system consists of the following components:

User → Ticket Creation → Flow Designer Trigger → Classification Logic → Ticket Update → Assignment Group → Support Team

The flow automatically processes the ticket after it satisfies the configured trigger conditions.

3.2 Flow Designer Components
The project can contain the following Flow Designer components:

Trigger
The flow is triggered when a ticket is:

Created, or

Updated based on defined conditions.

Actions
Possible actions include:

Look up ticket information.

Evaluate ticket fields.

Update ticket fields.

Assign the ticket to a support group.

Add work notes.

Send a notification when required.

Flow Logic
Conditions can be configured for different types of tickets.

For example:

Ticket Information	Classification	Assignment Group
Password reset	Access Issue	Service Desk
Laptop not working	Hardware Issue	Hardware Support
Application error	Software Issue	Application Support
Network unavailable	Network Issue	Network Support
Email problem	Email Issue	Messaging Support

3.3 Classification Logic
The classification process can use conditions based on keywords or existing ticket fields.

For example:

IF short description contains "password"
→ Category = Access Issue
→ Assignment Group = Service Desk

IF short description contains "laptop" or "keyboard"
→ Category = Hardware Issue
→ Assignment Group = Hardware Support

IF short description contains "application error"
→ Category = Software Issue
→ Assignment Group = Application Support

IF short description contains "network" or "Wi-Fi"
→ Category = Network Issue
→ Assignment Group = Network Support

ELSE
→ Category = General/Unclassified
→ Assignment Group = Service Desk
